---
required_variables:
  - runtime
  - runtime.agent
  - runtime.path
  - operation
  - correlation_id
  - params
metadata:
  id: agent-invocation
  version: 1.0.0
  purpose: Strict one-envelope invocation of a resolved plan-anchor agent
---
Invoke the resolved `{{ runtime.agent }}` definition at `{{ runtime.path }}` with the harness **Agent** tool. Pass exactly this one fenced JSON params object and no prose:

```json
{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "runtime": {{ runtime | tojson }},
  "operation": {{ operation | tojson }},
  "correlation_id": {{ correlation_id | tojson }},
  "params": {{ params | tojson }}
}
```

Accept exactly one fenced JSON result. Save the response unchanged and validate
it with `anchor_runner_contract.py validate-fence --kind result --file
<response-file> --correlation-id <correlation-id>`; use its data only when it
reports `data.valid: true` (`data.valid: false` names the `violation`).
